1. **A non-transitory computer-readable medium** storing instructions that, when executed by one or more processors of a mobile device having a camera and a display, cause the mobile device to perform operations comprising:

   establishing a wireless communication link with a lamp comprising a plurality of individually controllable light sources;

   causing the lamp to project, onto a surface, a light pattern comprising illumination from the plurality of individually controllable light sources and a plurality of marker lights associated with respective ones of the individually controllable light sources;

   capturing, using the camera of the mobile device, an image of the surface including the projected light pattern;

   processing the captured image to detect positions of the plurality of marker lights within the captured image;

   determining, based at least in part on the detected positions of the plurality of marker lights, corresponding image locations associated with the respective individually controllable light sources;

   generating a graphical user interface comprising the captured image and a plurality of selectable control elements overlaid on the captured image at the corresponding image locations; and

   in response to receiving a user selection of one of the selectable control elements on the display, transmitting, over the wireless communication link, a control command to the lamp to adjust an operating parameter of the individually controllable light source associated with the selected control element.

1. A user device comprising:  

a display;  

a camera interface configured to receive image data from a camera, the image data depicting a projected lamp pattern on a projection surface and a plurality of marker light sources having known positional relationships to the projected lamp pattern; and  

one or more processors coupled to the display and the camera interface, the one or more processors configured to execute an application that causes the user device to:  

identify, in the image data, respective image positions of the plurality of marker light sources;  

determine, based at least in part on the respective image positions of the plurality of marker light sources, a geometric distortion of the projected lamp pattern as viewed by the camera;  

generate a transformed control overlay by geometrically transforming a control overlay according to the determined geometric distortion; and  

present, on the display, the transformed control overlay aligned with the projected lamp pattern such that user-selectable controls of the transformed control overlay correspond to respective regions of the distorted projected lamp pattern.

1. A smartphone comprising:  
   a camera;  
   a display;  
   a wireless communication interface;  
   one or more processors; and  
   a non-transitory memory storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the smartphone to:  

   establish, via the wireless communication interface, communication with a controllable light-source array comprising a plurality of individually controllable light-emitting elements;  

   cause the display to present an image corresponding to a projection produced by the controllable light-source array;  

   receive, from the camera, image data representing at least a portion of the projection;  

   identify, in the image data, positions of marker lights associated with respective light-emitting elements of the controllable light-source array;  

   generate, based at least in part on the identified positions of the marker lights, an interactive overlay registered with the image of the projection, the interactive overlay including a plurality of selectable regions corresponding to individual light-emitting elements of the controllable light-source array;  

   receive a user input selecting at least one of the selectable regions of the interactive overlay; and  

   transmit, via the wireless communication interface, a control command to the controllable light-source array to adjust operation of a light-emitting element corresponding to the selected selectable region.

2. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein the control command adjusts at least one of an on/off state, brightness, color, color temperature, modulation pattern, or temporal activation sequence of the corresponding light-emitting element.

3. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein the marker lights are generated by selectively activating one or more predetermined light-emitting elements of the controllable light-source array according to a calibration pattern.

4. The smartphone of claim 3, wherein the calibration pattern comprises sequential activation of individual light-emitting elements, activation of corner light-emitting elements, activation of encoded groups of light-emitting elements, or a combination thereof.

5. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein the instructions further cause the smartphone to determine a geometric transform between coordinates of the controllable light-source array and coordinates of the image of the projection based on the identified positions of the marker lights.

6. The smartphone of claim 5, wherein the geometric transform comprises a homography, affine transform, perspective transform, or non-linear mapping.

7. The smartphone of claim 5, wherein the interactive overlay is registered with the image of the projection using the geometric transform such that user selection of a location on the display is mapped to a corresponding light-emitting element of the controllable light-source array.

8. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein the display presents a live camera view of the projection and the interactive overlay is superimposed on the live camera view.

9. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein the display presents a stored image, simulated image, or reconstructed image of the projection and the interactive overlay is superimposed on the stored image, simulated image, or reconstructed image.

10. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein the wireless communication interface comprises at least one of Bluetooth, Bluetooth Low Energy, Wi-Fi, near-field communication, ultra-wideband, infrared communication, or a cellular communication interface.

11. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein the controllable light-source array comprises an array of LEDs, micro-LEDs, laser diodes, organic LEDs, or individually addressable pixels.

12. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein the instructions further cause the smartphone to display, in association with the interactive overlay, a user interface control for changing a lighting parameter of the selected light-emitting element.

13. The smartphone of claim 12, wherein the user interface control comprises a color picker, brightness slider, toggle switch, pattern selector, timing control, or grouping control.

14. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein the instructions further cause the smartphone to define a group of light-emitting elements based on a user gesture applied to the interactive overlay and to transmit a group control command to adjust the group of light-emitting elements.

15. The smartphone of claim 14, wherein the user gesture comprises tapping, dragging, drawing a boundary, lasso selection, multi-touch selection, or swiping across a portion of the interactive overlay.

16. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein the instructions further cause the smartphone to update the interactive overlay in response to movement of the smartphone, movement of the controllable light-source array, or movement of a projection surface.

17. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein identifying the positions of the marker lights comprises detecting light spots having predetermined color, intensity, blinking frequency, temporal code, spatial arrangement, or optical signature.

18. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein the instructions further cause the smartphone to request the controllable light-source array to emit the marker lights prior to generating the interactive overlay.

19. The smartphone of claim 1, wherein the projection is cast onto an external surface separate from the smartphone.

20. A method performed by a smartphone, the method comprising:  
   establishing communication between the smartphone and a controllable light-source array comprising a plurality of individually controllable LEDs;  
   displaying, on a display of the smartphone, an image of a projection produced by the controllable light-source array;  
   acquiring, using a camera of the smartphone, image data of the projection;  
   detecting positions of marker lights in the image data;  
   correlating the detected positions of the marker lights with respective LEDs of the controllable light-source array;  
   presenting an interactive overlay on the displayed image of the projection, the interactive overlay including selectable overlay portions mapped to individual LEDs of the controllable light-source array;  
   receiving user input directed to one of the selectable overlay portions; and  
   sending a command from the smartphone to the controllable light-source array to control an individual LED corresponding to the one selectable overlay portion.

21. The method of claim 20, further comprising calculating a coordinate mapping between a coordinate system of the controllable light-source array and a coordinate system of the displayed image of the projection.

22. The method of claim 21, wherein the coordinate mapping is calculated from at least three detected marker-light positions.

23. The method of claim 20, wherein the command changes a lighting characteristic of the individual LED selected by the user through the interactive overlay.

24. The method of claim 20, further comprising causing the controllable light-source array to illuminate selected LEDs as marker lights according to a known calibration sequence.

25. The method of claim 20, further comprising visually indicating, on the interactive overlay, a current state of one or more LEDs of the controllable light-source array.

26. A non-transitory computer-readable medium storing instructions that, when executed by one or more processors of a smartphone, cause the smartphone to:  
   communicate with a controllable LED array;  
   obtain image data of a projection generated by the controllable LED array;  
   locate marker lights within the image data;  
   map locations of the marker lights to corresponding LEDs of the controllable LED array;  
   display an image of the projection with an overlay registered to the mapped locations;  
   receive a user selection of an overlay element corresponding to an individual LED; and  
   transmit a control signal to the controllable LED array to modify operation of the individual LED.

1. A system for controlling one or more lights, comprising:  

   a light source configured to project a predetermined light pattern onto a surface;  

   an image capture device configured to capture an image of the predetermined light pattern as distorted by the surface;  

   a plurality of marker light-emitting diodes disposed at known positions relative to the light source;  

   one or more processors configured to:  

   identify, in the captured image, the distorted predetermined light pattern and light emitted by the plurality of marker light-emitting diodes;  

   determine, based at least in part on the identified light emitted by the plurality of marker light-emitting diodes, a registration between the captured image and a control grid displayed by an application on a user interface;  

   map one or more regions of the captured image to corresponding control regions of the control grid using the registration;  

   receive a user selection of at least one of the corresponding control regions via the user interface; and  

   generate, in response to the user selection, a control command for adjusting an operating characteristic of at least one of the one or more lights.

1. A user device comprising:

a display;

a communication interface configured to communicate with a lamp comprising a plurality of controllable light sources;

a camera configured to capture an image of a projection surface illuminated by the lamp; and

one or more processors configured to execute an application to:

transmit, via the communication interface, control instructions to the lamp to cause the plurality of controllable light sources to project a light pattern including a plurality of markers onto the projection surface;

receive, from the camera, an image of the projected light pattern;

detect, in the image, respective locations of the plurality of markers;

determine, based on the detected respective locations of the plurality of markers, an alignment between the projection surface and an interactive control overlay; and

present, on the display, the interactive control overlay aligned according to the determined alignment, the interactive control overlay including one or more user-selectable controls for controlling at least one of the plurality of controllable light sources.
